    "body": "When `_IndexReader` reads metadata from an index header, it opens the `.idx` file once to read the header and again inside `numpy.memmap`. At large distributed-training scale, the extra open can add unnecessary metadata RPCs on distributed filesystems.\n\nCreate the memory map from the already-open file object inside the same context manager. The Python file object is closed after mapping, while the mapping keeps its existing lifetime and cleanup. The pre-supplied metadata path still opens the index only once.\n\nValidation:\n- Local CPU smoke check using the actual `DType` and `_IndexReader` class definitions extracted with AST, real NumPy mappings, and Python audit hooks: header-reading opens decrease from 2 to 1; pre-supplied metadata opens remain at 1.\n- Checked both text and multimodal indices, lengths/pointers/document indices/modes, indexed access, mapping cleanup, and invalid header/version rejection.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Full GPU unit tests were not run (no CUDA/container environment on this macOS host). `tools/autoformat.sh` was attempted but stopped because `black` is not installed.\n- No distributed-filesystem performance benchmark was run; the measured improvement is the removed file open.\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
    "closed_at": null,
